Tobias: Wish lanterns! Paper, a candle stub, and whatever you want to send up with it.
- I'll take a look.
	Tobias: After dark, carry one down to the table on the river bank and let it go.
	[signal arg="shop:festival"]
- What do people wish for?
	Tobias: Rain at the right time. Walls that hold. Someone coming home.
	Tobias: Mostly, I think, they wish the year goes as well as this evening.
- Goodnight.
	Tobias: Goodnight. Mind the creek in the dark.
